<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Seringapatam</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1792</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-anglo-mysore-war">Third Anglo-Mysore War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srirangapatna">Seringapatam</a> was signed in March 1792 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tipu-sultan">Tipu Sultan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a> with the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> and its allies, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizam-of-hyderabad">Nizam of Hyderabad</a>, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-anglo-mysore-war">Third Anglo-Mysore War</a>. With Cornwallis's army outside Srirangapatna, Tipu ceded about half of his territory, paid a heavy indemnity and handed over two of his sons as hostages.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-seringapatam.jpg" alt="Treaty of Seringapatam" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Miljoshi assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anglo-Mysore_War_3.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
